implementationPlan.description:
One shared fake proxy; the sh harness installs it.

Measure first, at the CURRENT HEAD after the three dependencies (5f3960df, 07474ee4, c2cb5cf7) have landed:
- sh body: `git show HEAD:scripts/tests/postflight.sh`, from after `cat > "$FAKE_PROXY" <<'JS'` through the next `\nJS\n`;
- ps1 body: `git show HEAD:scripts/tests/postflight.ps1`, from after `Set-Content -Path $fakeProxy -Encoding UTF8 -Value @'` through the next `\n'@`.
Normalize BOM and CRLF, then diff the two.

Before editing, post the per-hunk classification as a task comment; QA audits DoD 1 against it. Each hunk is one of:
- SHARED: one behaviour is kept, chosen to mirror the real daemon tool it fakes; cite the packages/moe-daemon/src/tools source.
- ENGINE-SPECIFIC: kept behind an explicit branch in the shared file, with a comment at the site giving the reason.

Architect's measurement at HEAD 1f9c7d5 (161 lines in about 20 hunks; re-check it, because the dependencies edit these bodies):
- helpers: ps1 has top-level readTask (strips the PS 5.1 Set-Content BOM), strList, declaredSets and csv; sh uses inline lambdas;
- resume alreadyAssigned: sh status is fixed REVIEW, ps1 uses FAKE_TASK_STATUS || REVIEW, and the reason text differs;
- BLOCKED hold: sh uses task-blocked with moe.wait_for_task, ps1 uses task-resume with moe.get_context;
- the get_context no-taskId adoption comment;
- placement of chat_send and heartbeat;
- two get_commit_scope implementations:
  - sh: FAKE_SCOPE_* lists APPEND; FAKE_SCOPE_PEERS_ACTIVE; alwaysInclude = own record + project.json + idle peers' records; preflight answers the record's own status;
  - ps1: lists OVERRIDE; peer entries split on the last ':'; peers' touchedFiles are included; alwaysInclude is [];
- record_commit: ps1 adds ensureDir and sha;
- declare_files: sh returns addedPaths;
- deregister_worker: sh logs deregister.log for scenario W.
Expected outcome: zero engine-specific branches, with the BOM strip shared (a no-op for sh).

Create scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js (LF) holding the union. Switch postflight.sh to `cp <repo root>/scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js "$FAKE_PROXY"`, using the harness's existing repo-root variable. Keep the $TMP_DIR/fake-proxy.js destination, so MOE_PROXY_PATH, the frozen-suite argument and any runtime edits still work on the copy.

Where a unified knob semantics changes what a sh scenario sees, adjust that scenario's SETUP, never its assertion about wrapper behaviour. Never copy one proxy wholesale over the other.

Rail: scripts/moe-agent.sh and .ps1 stay unchanged. If a harmonized fixture shows a wrapper behaving wrongly, keep that harness's old fixture behaviour behind a marked engine-specific branch, post the defect to #governors so it gets its own bug row, and continue.

Error handling: a failed cp must abort the harness (set -e).

implementationPlan.note:
Measured at HEAD b93702d after all four dependencies landed. sh body is 33517 B and ps1 body 31880 B (BOM and CRLF normalised); diff is 165 lines. The classification was posted before editing as comment-ed0ace77719d4bc3b3c5d81abd1af297: H1-H20 are all SHARED, with ZERO engine-specific branches.

New file scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js (LF, 34801 B, node --check OK):
- top-level readTask (with the BOM strip), strList, declaredSets (= collectTaskPathTiers) and csv;
- resume status is FAKE_TASK_STATUS || REVIEW;
- the BLOCKED hold uses task-resume with nextAction moe.report_blocked;
- get_commit_scope mirrors getCommitScope.ts:
  - asserted and planned come from the record;
  - peers come from the other open records in id order (first claimant wins), then FAKE_SCOPE_PEER_DECLARED is appended (split on the last ':');
  - FAKE_SCOPE_PEERS_ACTIVE and FAKE_SCOPE_PEER_ACTIVE are kept;
  - alwaysInclude = own record + project.json + non-live-peer records;
  - pre-flight answers the record's own status;
- FAKE_SCOPE_ASSERTED, FAKE_SCOPE_PLANNED and FAKE_SCOPE_ASSIGNED are dropped, because no harness sets them;
- record_commit gets ensureDir, sha and the filesModified/addedPaths lists;
- declare_files gets addedPaths;
- deregister_worker writes deregister.log (scenario W).

postflight.sh: the heredoc is replaced by `cp "$ROOT_DIR/scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js" "$FAKE_PROXY"`; a failed cp aborts the run under set -e. The temp destination is unchanged, so MOE_PROXY_PATH and the frozen argv see the copy. Scenario SETUPS only: task-blocked becomes task-resume (32 sites, plus 'Blocked smoke' becomes 'Resume smoke') in Mb, M2 b-e, M3d and AB2. No wrapper assertion was changed. Diff is +33/-567.

parity-check.sh fix: the ps1 install check now greps the file directly. The old `tr | grep -q` pipe died with SIGPIPE 141 under pipefail. parity-check.sh, and parity-check.ps1 on PS 5.1 and pwsh 7, pass on snapshot D:\moe-scratch\7c28-s1.

Verification: `MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=180 bash scripts/tests/postflight.sh` from snapshot /tmp/moe-7c28/snap-sh1 (git archive HEAD plus the owned files overlaid; MOE_*/CLAUDE* unset). It ran 05:21:10Z-05:30:48Z with rc 0 and printed PASS postflight.sh. Counts: frozen candidate 73 and scope 38 (A..AF, excluding the P2 sub-runs, Q and V), equal to c2cb5cf7's recorded counts. scripts/moe-agent.sh and scripts/moe-agent.ps1 were not touched, nor any peer's dirty paths.

implementationPlan.description:
One adversarial self-review of this task's diff (load adversarial-self-review). Check that:
- every hunk in the posted classification comment is accounted for in postflight-fake-proxy.js;
- every FAKE_* knob either harness sets is still read by the shared proxy (grep both harnesses against it: a knob that is set but never read is a lost scenario), and every knob the proxy reads is documented in DEVELOPMENT.md;
- no assertion was weakened to fit the union;
- ps1 records written with a BOM still parse;
- the frozen suite still receives the copied proxy path;
- the parity group cannot pass vacuously: a mention in a comment while a private body remains must still fail, so match install sites;
- `git diff --stat` shows scripts/moe-agent.sh and scripts/moe-agent.ps1 untouched, and no peer's dirty bytes are touched.

The diff is mostly a move, so net LOC is negative. Name the classification comment id in the completion summary so QA can audit the shared file against both old bodies.
